{"id": "EUVD-2026-85342", "enisaUuid": "591c6477-f325-3ef1-9252-1785f01726ed", "description": "A malicious or compromised Flatpak repository can write attacker-controlled content to arbitrary locations on the host filesystem via extract_extra_data(). On system installs, the write happens as root. Two issues combine: `files/extra` is resolved via path operations that follow symlinks, and blob names from `xa.extra-data-sources` are not sanitized against `..` traversal.", "datePublished": "2026-09-23T15:01:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-12T16:25:35", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80497", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80498", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80687", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-96275", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2539416", "https://github.com/flatpak/flatpak/security/advisories/GHSA-fqx6-vh4p-42cg"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-96275"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6d716816-6e63-3f86-a620-d10d4bf1dff8", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.16.0-9.el10_2.4"}, {"id": "8b238fee-e15a-3905-a332-6efa0286db83", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.12.9-7.el8_10"}, {"id": "b64d87d3-29eb-389e-94e4-60bb90c5593e", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.12.9-4.el9_8.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c205504a-dc72-3396-8b90-ddc1de8d9d85", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}], "isExploited": false}